# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment variables — PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never put real values in this file.
#
# This is the one .env file that IS committed (see the negation in .gitignore).
# It exists to document the required names. To work locally, copy it and fill it
# in — or, better, pull the real values straight from Vercel:
#
#     cp .env.local.example .env.local
#     vercel env pull .env.local        # overwrites with the real values
#
# .env.local is gitignored and will never be committed.
#
# Everything here is consumed by /birthday alone. The rest of the site needs no
# configuration at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Storage: Upstash Redis, via Vercel Storage ───────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ CUSTOM PREFIX. @vercel/kv auto-detects only the unprefixed
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN. This project's store is provisioned with
# an AYODELE_ prefix, so app/api/birthday-testimony/route.ts passes these to
# createClient() explicitly. Renaming them breaks the route.
#
# Required — testimonies cannot be stored or read without these.
AYODELE_KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-store-name.upstash.io
AYODELE_KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-read-write-token

# Optional. The GET handler prefers this so a read cannot mutate the list.
#
# ⚠️ LEAVE IT COMMENTED OUT unless you paste the REAL token. The fallback to
# the read/write token above only fires when this variable is UNSET. A
# placeholder value is "set", so it wins — and every read then fails with
# "WRONGPASS invalid or missing auth token". An absent variable works; a
# wrong one breaks GET.
# AYODELE_KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN=your-read-only-token

# Set by Vercel, not used by this codebase. Both are redis:// connection
# strings for a TCP client; @vercel/kv speaks the REST protocol. Documented so
# nobody wastes time wondering why they appear unused.
# AYODELE_KV_URL=rediss://...
# AYODELE_REDIS_URL=rediss://...


# ── Admin gate for /birthday/admin ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ Deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. It is compared server-side, in
# app/api/birthday-admin/route.ts. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is inlined into the
# browser bundle and readable by every visitor — which for a password means
# publishing it.
BIRTHDAY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-password


# ── Email notifications: Resend ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Entirely optional. Without RESEND_API_KEY the email step is skipped and the
# testimony is still stored — KV is the record, email is a convenience.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_api_key

# Where testimony notifications are sent.
# Defaults to contact@ayodeleaweministries.org when unset.
BIRTHDAY_NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# ⚠️ Resend only sends from a domain you have VERIFIED. Until
# ayodeleaweministries.org is verified, the only usable sender is
# onboarding@resend.dev — and in that mode Resend delivers ONLY to the address
# that owns the Resend account, so BIRTHDAY_NOTIFY_EMAIL must be that address.
# Defaults to "AOA Ministries <onboarding@resend.dev>" when unset.
BIRTHDAY_EMAIL_FROM=


# ── Site URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Makes og:image absolute — WhatsApp and Facebook will not fetch a relative
# path. Falls back to VERCEL_URL, then localhost. Set this once the custom
# domain is pointed at Vercel.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
